<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="dimensions-overview" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Six Dimensions of Culturally Responsive Teaching</title>

  <introduction>
    <figure xml:id="Diagram-Six-DimensionsCRT">
      <caption>The six dimensions of culturally responsive teaching</caption>
      <image source="Diagram-Six-DimensionsCRT.png">
        <shortdescription>Six numbered hexagons ringing a center labeled Youth empowerment, each pointing inward.</shortdescription>
        <description>
          <p>
            Six colored hexagons are arranged in a ring, numbered 1 through 6: Students at the
            Center, Relationships and caring, Deep thinking, Access and relevance, Social justice
            reflection, and Inclusion through cultural diversity. An arrow points inward from each
            hexagon to a green splash at the center labeled <q>Youth empowerment</q>, which is
            encircled by a band labeled <q>Curriculum</q>.
          </p>
        </description>
      </image>
    </figure>
    <p>
      These six dimensions aim to capture the essence of Culturally Responsive Teaching in our
      informal math enrichment program (and we believe that can be helpful for other programs).
      Each dimension corresponds to a hexagon in the diagram. We also describe the
      <q>fundamental goal</q> of our program (in the center of the diagram), as well as the three
      general contexts in which the six dimensions materialize (the concentric circles).
    </p>

    <p>
      <dl>
        <li><title>The main goal</title>
          <p>Personal Development &amp; Growth</p>
        </li>
        <li><title>The three contexts</title>
          <p>Program structure, Pedagogical practices, Curriculum</p>
        </li>
        <li><title>The six dimensions</title>
          <p>
            <ol>
              <li>Students at the center</li>
              <li>Relationships and caring</li>
              <li>Deep thinking</li>
              <li>Access and relevance</li>
              <li>Inclusion through cultural diversity</li>
              <li>Social justice reflection</li>
            </ol>
          </p>
        </li>
      </dl>
    </p>

  </introduction>

  <subsection xml:id="dimensions-summary">
    <title>Overview of the Six Dimensions</title>

    <paragraphs>
      <title>Dimension 1: Students at the center</title>
      <p>
        <dl width="wide">
          <li><title>1.1 Adapt to students' worlds</title>
            <p>Design and adjust activities based on students' cultures, interests, and real-time engagement.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>1.2 Guide learning continuously</title>
            <p>Anticipate, observe, question, and support students to address needs and advance understanding.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>1.3 Foster students' interactions</title>
            <p>Foster collaboration as students move from individual thinking to sharing and reasoning together.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>1.4 Integrate concepts and contexts</title>
            <p>Link student ideas, previous understanding, and different contexts to consolidate the learning goals.</p>
          </li>
        </dl>
      </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
      <title>Dimension 2: Relationships and caring</title>
      <p>
        <dl width="wide">
          <li><title>2.1 Welcome every student</title>
            <p>Use your words and actions to create a positive, welcoming space where meaningful learning can happen.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>2.2 Find ways to connect</title>
            <p>Encourage meaningful and constant two-way exchanges with students.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>2.3 Build confidence and trust</title>
            <p>Help students trust themselves, you, and the learning process.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>2.4 Be a role model</title>
            <p>Show students how to approach challenges, think critically, and behave in a responsible way.</p>
          </li>
        </dl>
      </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
      <title>Dimension 3: Deep thinking</title>
      <p>
        <dl width="wide">
          <li><title>3.1 Prepare for deep ideas and connections</title>
            <p>Get ready so that activities are geared toward deep reasoning and making connections.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>3.2 Pave the way for deep thinking</title>
            <p>Create a learning environment to encourage students to reason, notice patterns, and connect thinking.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>3.3 Support reasoning strategically</title>
            <p>Help students clarify their thinking, scaffold their reasoning, and overcome conceptual challenges.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>3.4 Guide through challenges</title>
            <p>Encourage persistence, resilience, and productive struggle in problem-solving.</p>
          </li>
        </dl>
      </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
      <title>Dimension 4: Access and relevance</title>
      <p>
        <dl width="wide">
          <li><title>4.1 Include meaningful tasks</title>
            <p>Present activities that connect to students' cultures and lives, and spark curiosity.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>4.2 Use accessible language</title>
            <p>Explain clearly, and allow diverse language and communication.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>4.3 Introduce powerful representations</title>
            <p>Use manipulatives, visuals, and models effectively to build understanding.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>4.4 Use modalities flexibly</title>
            <p>Help students choose and adapt ways to represent ideas and systems.</p>
          </li>
        </dl>
      </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
      <title>Dimension 5: Inclusion through cultural diversity</title>
      <p>
        <dl width="wide">
          <li><title>5.1 Honor cultural identities</title>
            <p>Value who students are and where they come from, showing pride in their cultures and making their practices visible.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>5.2 Tie content with culture</title>
            <p>Intentionally connect teaching content to cultural experiences, world scenarios, and diverse perspectives.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>5.3 Implement inclusive practices</title>
            <p>Design learning spaces and activities where all voices, traditions, and cultural ways of learning feel welcome.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>5.4 Promote respect and critical awareness</title>
            <p>Guide students beyond their comfort zones to explore unfamiliar cultures, discuss differences respectfully, and challenge stereotypes.</p>
          </li>
        </dl>
      </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
      <title>Dimension 6: Social justice reflection</title>
      <p>
        <dl width="wide">
          <li><title>6.1 Cultivate empathy and awareness</title>
            <p>Help students see different perspectives through data, games, and real-world simulations.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>6.2 Examine fairness and justice</title>
            <p>Guide students to spot systemic inequity and use math to explore what fairness looks like in real life.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>6.3 Connect math to real-world impact</title>
            <p>Use math modeling to analyze inequalities and drive practical solutions.</p>
          </li>
          <li><title>6.4 Inspire agency toward change</title>
            <p>Empower students to use math insights to advocate for community solutions and drive meaningful change.</p>
          </li>
        </dl>
      </p>
    </paragraphs>
  </subsection>

</section>
